{"name":"Fluffy Slippers","hex":"#d8e5e4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fluffy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Covered with fluff.","Light; soft; airy."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone or something that has a fluffy texture.","A person who is superficial, who lacks depth or seriousness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fluffy"},{"term":"slippers","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of slipper"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of slipper"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slippers"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fluffy (footwear)","blocks":[{"text":"A fluffy, also known as a furry leg warmer or furry boot cover, is a type of footwear fashion accessory. It is a variation on a leg warmer normally made out of faux fur that covers the user's main footwear. It is commonly associated with cybergoth fashion and the rave scene. Fluffies originated in the Ibiza rave scene of the mid-to-late-1990s, where podium dancers wore them during their performances."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Girl_in_cyber_costume_at_Katsucon_2013.jpg/330px-Girl_in_cyber_costume_at_Katsucon_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fluffy_(footwear)"},{"title":"Slipper","blocks":[{"text":"Slippers are a type of shoes falling under the broader category of light footwear, that are easy to put on and off and are intended to be worn indoors, particularly at home. They provide comfort and protection for the feet when walking indoors."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Slippers.jpg/330px-Slippers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slipper"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/2016_Singapur%2C_Downtown_Co